# Sekant resource sizing
#
# Append the block matching your host to .env, then restart the stack.
#
# By default no container has a memory limit, which is how installs behaved before these settings
# existed. Limits only apply when you set them here. That is deliberate: every file in
# distribution-manifest.txt, including docker-compose.yml, is REPLACED by
# `sekant_server.sh --upgrade`, while .env is kept. A hard-coded default in docker-compose.yml would
# silently resize every existing install on its next upgrade, including hosts far larger than the
# default assumed.
#
# ClickHouse is protected even without a container limit: clickhouse/config.d/limits.xml caps its
# memory at a fraction of host RAM (or of CLICKHOUSE_MEM_LIMIT when set) and caps its caches.
#
# Capacity depends far more on the dashboard response size than on user count. Until the payload
# reduction lands, treat these tiers as containment, not as a capacity promise. See
# docs/security-events-performance-plan.md.
#
# BACKEND heap: --max-old-space-size bounds only the V8 heap. The dashboard path also holds
# response Buffers, decoded strings and socket buffers outside the heap, measured at roughly one
# payload-sized spike per in-flight cold request. When heap plus off-heap memory exceeds
# BACKEND_MEM_LIMIT the process is killed silently (exit 137, no log). The heap values below leave
# about 40% of the container for that; in testing, 78% left too little room at small sizes.
#
# REDIS: keep REDIS_MEM_LIMIT at least REDIS_MAXMEMORY x 1.05 plus the largest cached value plus
# 64 MiB. Today's largest dashboard entry is about 118-134 MiB.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8 GB / 2 vCPU  — evaluation only, below the supported minimum
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLICKHOUSE_MEM_LIMIT=2560m
# BACKEND_MEM_LIMIT=1536m
# BACKEND_NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=896
# REDIS_MEM_LIMIT=640m
# REDIS_MAXMEMORY=384mb
# KEYCLOAK_MEM_LIMIT=1024m
# POSTGRES_MEM_LIMIT=768m
# SQL_VALIDATOR_MEM_LIMIT=256m
# CADDY_MEM_LIMIT=384m
# NGINX_MEM_LIMIT=384m

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 16 GB / 4 vCPU
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLICKHOUSE_MEM_LIMIT=4608m
# BACKEND_MEM_LIMIT=4096m
# BACKEND_NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=2432
# REDIS_MEM_LIMIT=2048m
# REDIS_MAXMEMORY=1536mb
# KEYCLOAK_MEM_LIMIT=1536m
# POSTGRES_MEM_LIMIT=1536m
# SQL_VALIDATOR_MEM_LIMIT=384m
# CADDY_MEM_LIMIT=512m
# NGINX_MEM_LIMIT=512m

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 32 GB / 8 vCPU  — documented minimum
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLICKHOUSE_MEM_LIMIT=9472m
# BACKEND_MEM_LIMIT=9216m
# BACKEND_NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=5504
# REDIS_MEM_LIMIT=4608m
# REDIS_MAXMEMORY=3584mb
# KEYCLOAK_MEM_LIMIT=2048m
# POSTGRES_MEM_LIMIT=2048m
# SQL_VALIDATOR_MEM_LIMIT=512m
# CADDY_MEM_LIMIT=512m
# NGINX_MEM_LIMIT=512m

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 64 GB / 16 vCPU
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLICKHOUSE_MEM_LIMIT=17920m
# BACKEND_MEM_LIMIT=19456m
# BACKEND_NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=11520
# REDIS_MEM_LIMIT=8704m
# REDIS_MAXMEMORY=7gb
# KEYCLOAK_MEM_LIMIT=4096m
# POSTGRES_MEM_LIMIT=4096m
# SQL_VALIDATOR_MEM_LIMIT=768m
# CADDY_MEM_LIMIT=768m
# NGINX_MEM_LIMIT=768m

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Proxy limits (CADDY_MEM_LIMIT, NGINX_MEM_LIMIT) must carry the full dashboard response while it
# streams. At today's 128 MB payload, a 64 MiB nginx was killed five times mid-response in testing.
# Do not shrink these below the values above until the payload reduction ships.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redis eviction. docker-compose.yml already defaults to REDIS_MAXMEMORY=3584mb with allkeys-lru.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redis ships upstream with `noeviction`, which REJECTS writes once memory is exhausted rather
# than evicting. That fails every cache write simultaneously instead of degrading. An evicted
# dashboard entry costs one re-query; an unbounded Redis costs the host.
# REDIS_MAXMEMORY_POLICY=allkeys-lru
